Entropy of vaporisation ( $\Delta$ S)
$$
=\frac{\text { enthalpy of vaporisation }(\Delta H)}{\text { boiling point (in K)} }
$$
Given, $\Delta H=24.64 \mathrm{kJ} \mathrm{mol}^{-1}$ and
$\text { boiling point }=35+273=308 \mathrm{k}$
$\therefore$
$$
\begin{aligned}
\Delta S &=\frac{24.64 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{J} \mathrm{mol}^{-1}}{308 \mathrm{K}} \\
&=80 \mathrm{JK}^{-1} \mathrm{mol}^{-1}
\end{aligned}
$$
